{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777522193,"nonce":"ybU3B1z2MMBrq142HGC28LTw7is=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA5fb-A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/110","origin":"github"},"title":"urdf: model SBG INS, GNSS antenna(s), and IMU mounting alignment on bizzyboat","message":"## Summary\n\nThe BizzyBoat URDF (`bizzyboat_project11/urdf/bizzyboat.urdf.xacro`) does not\nmodel the SBG Ellipse-D INS, its mounting, or its GNSS antenna(s). A field\ncross-check on the 2026-04-29 in-water bag against the FCU EKF3 stream made\nthe missing geometry visible: the SBG and FCU are publishing position from\n**different physical points** without the URDF capturing where either of them\nsits.\n\n## Evidence (2026-04-29 in-water session)\n\nBag: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-29T21-43-29+00-00` (2 h 11 min, in water).\nDecomposing SBG `ekf_nav` − mavros `global_position/raw/fix` into vehicle body\nframe (using SBG yaw NED→ENU as a reference for body orientation):\n\n| axis (body, SBG − MAV) | median (moving \u003e0.7 m/s) | std |\n|---|---|---|\n| forward (bow+) | **−0.635 m** | 0.108 m |\n| port (left+)   | +0.020 m  | 0.048 m |\n| vertical       | +0.024 m¹ | 0.024 m |\n\n¹ after removing a steady +31.000 m geoid offset (SBG ellipsoidal vs mavros\nMSL — datum, not lever arm).\n\nWorld-frame horizontal std is **0.628 m**, body-frame is **0.119 m** — a 5×\ncollapse, which is the unambiguous signature of a **fixed body-frame lever\narm** rather than GPS noise or origin drift.\n\nRoll bias is also steady at **+1.79°** (SBG − MAV, std 0.17°). That is\nconsistent with an SBG IMU mounting-orientation offset that no part of the\nTF tree currently describes.\n\n## What's modelled today\n\n```\nbizzy/gnss_forward  at base_link  (+0.835, 0, +0.89)   # FCU primary\nbizzy/gnss_aft      at base_link  (−0.835, 0, +0.89)   # FCU secondary\nbizzy/imu           at base_link  (~−0.99, 0, +0.05)   # Cube Orange\n```\n\nNo `bizzy/sbg_imu`, no `bizzy/sbg_gnss_*`. Most consistent reading of the\n0.64 m fore-aft offset: mavros publishes at `gnss_forward`, SBG publishes at\nits own GNSS antenna at roughly **+0.20 m** on the centre rail (same height\nas the FCU pucks, since the vertical residual is 24 mm). But this is\ninferred geometry — the URDF is the authoritative source and right now it\nis silent.\n\n## Proposed scope\n\n- Add `bizzy/sbg_imu` link with measured pose relative to `base_link`,\n  including the orientation (the +1.79° roll bias suggests the IMU's body\n  axes aren't exactly aligned to base_link).\n- Add `bizzy/sbg_gnss_forward` (and `_aft` if/when the moving-base second\n  antenna is in use) for the SBG's own GNSS antenna(s).\n- Note in the URDF where each measurement is sourced from (manual/photo\n  measurement, with a date) so future agents can audit.\n\nThis issue is documentation/modelling only. Lever-arm correction of the\nposition streams to base_link is a separate, downstream concern — see the\ncompanion lever-arm issue.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `ros2 run tf2_tools view_frames` on a live or replayed bag should show\n  the SBG IMU and antenna frames present.\n- A repeat of the body-frame offset analysis on a future deployment, with\n  consumers using the new TFs to project to base_link, should drive the\n  body-frame offset toward zero (within GPS CEP of each antenna).\n\n## References\n\n- Deployment-day cross-check writeup: `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-29_dev_logs.md`\n  (timeline entry 2026-04-30T00:06-04:00).\n- Source bag: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-29T21-43-29+00-00`.\n\nPart of #104.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}